      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "DfkT9nfVG57a"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**CCS2313 Lab 6 Report — Time Series & Forecasting**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "sTRTc30vHDkq"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Step 1: Dataset Basics**\n",
        "\n",
        "Q1. How many monthly observations? → 24\n",
        "\n",
        "Q2. Time interval between observations? → 1 month\n",
        "\n",
        "Q3. Overall trend? → Upward trend (sales increase over time, despite fluctuations)."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "vFHVn04dHJCZ"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Step 2: Visualization**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "FAF7pKejHP55"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 407
        },
        "id": "7SNYdjg3G3mq",
        "outputId": "d0984108-c4ef-4fcb-b3a7-2143141515d8"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 900x400 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "data = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        " 'Month': pd.date_range('2024-01-01', periods=24, freq='MS'),\n",
        " 'Sales': [120,128,135,142,150,158,165,160,\n",
        "           155,168,180,195,138,145,153,162,\n",
        "           172,180,188,182,176,192,205,220]\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(9,4))\n",
        "plt.plot(data['Month'], data['Sales'], marker='o')\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Month'); plt.ylabel('Sales')\n",
        "plt.title('Monthly Store Sales')\n",
        "plt.xticks(rotation=45); plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Q4. Long-term pattern: Upward trend.\n",
        "\n",
        "Q5. Are changes smooth? No, short-term irregular fluctuations exist.\n",
        "\n",
        "Q6. Why order matters? Time-series depends on chronological sequence; shuffling breaks meaning."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Tsu1UvD8HisR"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Step 3: Moving Average Smoothing**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "iSn6eCEbHqeA"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "data['MA_3'] = data['Sales'].rolling(window=3).mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(9,4))\n",
        "plt.plot(data['Month'], data['Sales'], marker='o', label='Actual Sales')\n",
        "plt.plot(data['Month'], data['MA_3'], marker='o', label='3-Month MA')\n",
        "plt.legend(); plt.xticks(rotation=45); plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 407
        },
        "id": "Aac9gRRiHj9h",
        "outputId": "a0f2a0a9-cf76-4ac4-ad92-9d0b3977dda2"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 900x400 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Q7. Why first two missing? Need 3 values to compute average.\n",
        "\n",
        "Q8. Is MA smoother? Yes, reduces noise and highlights trend."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "uNVUeYTQHxuB"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Step 4: Moving-Average Forecast**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "LkswhEW3H1DY"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "last_3 = data['Sales'].tail(3)\n",
        "ma_forecast = last_3.mean()\n",
        "print(last_3.tolist(), round(ma_forecast,2))\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "FTKGi9L5HyyL",
        "outputId": "6c5c752f-0672-41ab-e898-45a644df2c65"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[192, 205, 220] 205.67\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Q9. Last 3 values used: 192, 205, 220\n",
        "\n",
        "Q10. Forecast for Jan 2026: (192+205+220)/3 = 205.67 ≈ 206\n",
        "\n",
        "Experiment with 6-month MA:\n",
        "\n",
        "Q11. Smoother line: 6-month MA\n",
        "\n",
        "Q12. Larger window: More smoothing, less sensitivity to short-term changes."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "KYob4hjzH8Ao"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Step 5: Sliding Window (Lag Features)**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8PvN4wqPH9Op"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "data['Lag_1'] = data['Sales'].shift(1)\n",
        "data['Lag_2'] = data['Sales'].shift(2)\n",
        "data['Lag_3'] = data['Sales'].shift(3)\n",
        "\n",
        "supervised = data.dropna(subset=['Lag_1','Lag_2','Lag_3']).copy()\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "QqQGb3ndIDFZ"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Q13. Lag_1: Previous month’s sales.\n",
        "\n",
        "Q14. First 3 rows unusable: Not enough lag values.\n",
        "\n",
        "Q15. Inputs X = Lag_1, Lag_2, Lag_3; Output y = Sales."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5svKZzMcIGpI"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Step 6: Train ML Forecasting Model**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "nJ6z5fEGIJMY"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n",
        "\n",
        "features = ['Lag_1','Lag_2','Lag_3']\n",
        "train = supervised.iloc[:-5]\n",
        "test = supervised.iloc[-5:]\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train, y_train = train[features], train['Sales']\n",
        "X_test, y_test = test[features], test['Sales']\n",
        "\n",
        "model = LinearRegression()\n",
        "model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "predictions = model.predict(X_test)\n",
        "\n",
        "results = test[['Month','Sales']].copy()\n",
        "results['Predicted_Sales'] = predictions\n",
        "results\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 206
        },
